<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Laser lifts interim headline shr, no div.</title>
<headline>Laser lifts interim headline shr, no div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		  25.2	  vs     19.3</p>
<p>    - attrib		    23.3	  vs     19.8 loss</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		    nil	  vs     nil</p>
<p>    Attrib income	     4.20	  vs     3.57 loss</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		     4.20	  vs     10.33 loss</p>
<p>    Tax			    nil	  vs     6.77</p>
<p>    Interest paid	     8.24	  vs     10.98</p>
<p>    Turnover		  116.85	  vs     141.26</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	 0.34	  vs     10.38 loss</p>
<p>Full name: Laser Transport Holdings Ltd (transportation)</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said no taxation had been provided for because the group's assessed losses exceeded the deferred tax liability.</p>
<p>It said profits in the second half of the year were traditionally lower than those in the first half but significant imprvement was seen for the six months to March 1998.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
